cygnet-provider (0.1.5-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Build the provider module with a platform-correct suffix. CMake gives
    MODULE libraries a .so suffix everywhere, but OpenSSL dlopens provider
    modules as .dylib on Darwin and .dll on Windows, so the macOS build could
    not be loaded without a manual symlink. A single CYGNET_MODULE_SUFFIX
    variable now drives both the built filename and the generated test
    configuration.
  * Skip tests/mac_forward_test (SKIP_RETURN_CODE 77) where no FIPS provider
    is present, instead of failing, so source builds succeed on hosts that
    ship no FIPS module.
  * Replace the hardcoded Ubuntu FIPS module path in the generated test
    configuration with the CYGNET_FIPS_MODULE cache variable.
  * Remove the unreferenced duplicate tests/openssl-cygnet-test.cnf.in.
  * Install the module to /usr/lib/<triplet>/ossl-modules/cygnetprov.so
    rather than /usr/lib. Provider modules must live on a filesystem mounted
    without noexec; dlopen otherwise fails with "failed to map segment from
    shared object", which names neither the module nor the mount.
  * Declare ninja-build in Build-Depends. debian/rules has always configured
    with -G Ninja, so the package could not build in a clean chroot.
  * No Debian package was released for 0.1.3 or 0.1.4.

 -- Sanctum SecOps LLC <support@sanctumsecops.com>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:30:00 +0000

cygnet-provider (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Wire the four CYGNET MAC algorithms into the provider build and dispatch.
    In 0.1.1 cygnetprov_mac.c was absent from the CMake source list, the
    cygnet_mac_algorithms symbol had no extern declaration, and
    query_operation had no OSSL_OP_MAC case, so CYGNET-HMAC, CYGNET-CMAC,
    CYGNET-KMAC-128, and CYGNET-KMAC-256 were unreachable at runtime.
  * Correct the provider-reported version string, which read 0.1.0 in the
    0.1.1 release.

 -- Sanctum SecOps LLC <support@sanctumsecops.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:41:00 +0000

